Backup generators are essential components of data center power infrastructure, providing electricity when the utility grid fails or becomes unreliable. These systems help protect critical computing equipment, maintain service availability, and reduce the risk of costly operational interruptions.

As cloud computing, digital services, and AI applications expand, data center operators are investing in reliable backup power systems with sufficient capacity, fast response, and redundant configurations. Generator selection increasingly involves fuel availability, emissions compliance, maintenance requirements, and integration with uninterruptible power supplies (UPS) and other power-management equipment.

